#10. Few-Shot Dynamic Template for Classification
Topics: Medium, Few-Shot, Classification

Scenario: You are classifying complex technical support tickets into sub-categories (DB_OUTAGE, PERMISSION_ERROR, NETWORK_LATENCY, DEPRECATED_API). Zero-shot 
prompts keep confusing DB_OUTAGE with NETWORK_LATENCY.

Task: Create a 3-shot prompt with edge-case examples that clearly demarcates subtle diagnostic differences.

Suggested Prompt / Solution Architecture:

          <SYSTEM_PROMPT>
          Classify technical support tickets into exactly one category: [DB_OUTAGE, PERMISSION_ERROR, NETWORK_LATENCY, DEPRECATED_API].
          
          EXAMPLES:
          Input: "Database pool connections timing out after 30000ms. Writes failing across all nodes."
          Thought: Connection pool timeouts driven by total write failure indicates primary node unreachable.
          Category: DB_OUTAGE
          
          Input: "API endpoint /v1/users returns HTTP 410 Gone with response body 'endpoint sunset on Jan 1'."
          Thought: HTTP 410 explicit sunset message refers to retired API versions.
          Category: DEPRECATED_API
          
          Input: "Queries executing fine locally, but cloud latency spiked from 20ms to 4500ms over cross-region VPC."
          Thought: High latency across VPC peering without database write failures indicates network transit bottleneck.
          Category: NETWORK_LATENCY
          
          <USER_INPUT>
          "Our cluster writes are succeeding fine, but read replicas across the east region are taking 12 seconds to sync."
          Category:

Engineering Insight: Few-shot examples with intermediate 'Thought:' explanations teach the model how to differentiate subtle distinctions between overlapping categories.
